      <Comment>The C&lt;sub&gt;28&lt;/sub&gt; brassinosteroid |FRAME: CPD-697| (BL) is the most biologically active and together with its C&lt;sub&gt;28&lt;/sub&gt; congeners is distributed widely in the plant kingdom |CITS:[15012241]|. Brassinolide was the first isolated brassinosteroid, when pollen from |FRAME: TAX-3708| was shown to promote stem elongation and cell divisions, and the biologically active molecule was isolated |CITS: [Grove79]|.</Comment>
